  {"i":601,"keep":[],"n":"'grasp the meaning' (要点をつかむ) is a figurative extension; teach in actions only"},
  {"i":622,"keep":[4],"n":"visiting a shrine or grave (お墓に参る) is a common sense taught with customs; 'stumped' (参った) is an exclamation, not an emotion-unit word"},
  {"i":631,"keep":[3],"n":"意見がぶつかる (opinions clash) is common at N3 and fits getting on with others"},
  {"i":632,"keep":[],"n":"the イッキ drinking chant is party slang; learners meet 一気に 'all at once'"},
  {"i":634,"keep":[],"n":"learners meet くそ as a curse; excrement is not taught in the body unit with this word"},
  {"i":666,"keep":[2],"n":"電話/ネットがつながる is very common and belongs to technology; 血がつながる is a narrower extension, so drop the family entry"},
  {"i":689,"keep":[4],"n":"服や靴がきつい (too tight) is a core clothing-unit sense"},
  {"i":692,"keep":[2],"n":"おじさん meaning 'middle-aged man, mister' is very common and belongs to people"},
  {"i":695,"keep":[2],"n":"しつこい味 (heavy, greasy) is taught with あっさり and こってり in food"},
  {"i":701,"keep":[2],"n":"holidays and days off (夏休み, 学校が休み) are taught in the school and travel units too"},
